# NestGlow Co — environment variables
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for local development, and set the same names in Vercel's
# project settings for production. `.env.local` is gitignored; this file is not,
# so never put a real value in here.
#
# NOTHING HERE IS REQUIRED FOR THE SITE TO WORK. The lead path runs without any
# of it: /api/lead forwards to Formspree, Caroline gets the email, the visitor
# sees the success screen. These only add the customer's confirmation receipt
# and Caroline's SMS alert.

# ── Resend: the customer's confirmation email ────────────────────────────
# The receipt the CUSTOMER gets. NOT Caroline's copy of the lead — that arrives
# by Formspree and is confirmed working (2026-08-23). Resend is additive: with
# these unset, `sendConfirmation` returns "skipped: …", the lead is still
# delivered, and the skip is logged. A missing receipt is never an error the
# visitor sees.
#
# Free tier is 3,000 emails/month, far above anything this site will send.

# resend.com/api-keys. Sending permission only — it never needs to read.
RESEND_API_KEY=

# The From header, display name included:
#   NestGlow Co <hello@send.nestglowco.com>
#
# ⚠️ USE A SUBDOMAIN, NEVER THE ROOT DOMAIN. Resend needs its own SPF and DKIM
# records on whatever it sends from. Putting those on `nestglowco.com` itself
# would collide with the records carrying Caroline's own mailbox
# (nestglowco@gmail.com). The `send.` subdomain keeps the two senders out of
# each other's way. Same shape Gorsegner (send.gorsegnerbrothers.com, verified
# 2026-08-16) and BDF both use.
#
# ── WHERE THE DNS RECORDS GO ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Hostinger's DNS Zone Editor, for now: nestglowco.com is still served by
# Hostinger and still points at the OLD site. Adding records for a `send.`
# subdomain does NOT require the site migration to happen first — the subdomain
# is independent of where the root domain points, so this can be set up before
# the DNS cutover and will survive it.
#
# After the cutover the zone may move; if it does, recreate these records
# wherever the zone then lives. Verify the domain in Resend BEFORE setting this
# value — an unverified domain returns a 403 and every receipt silently fails.
#
# Replies go to BUSINESS.email via reply_to, so a customer answering the receipt
# reaches Caroline rather than a no-reply address.
RESEND_FROM=


# ── Zapier: Caroline's SMS alert ─────────────────────────────────────────
# The "Catch Hook" URL from the Zap's trigger step. Looks like:
#   https://hooks.zapier.com/hooks/catch/1234567/abcdef/
#
# What it does: /api/lead POSTs one flat JSON object here the instant the
# contact form is submitted. The Zap texts it to Caroline via SMS by Zapier.
# Same pattern as Karla's quiz, without the Google Sheet in the middle, so there
# is no polling delay.
#
# It was WhatsApp first and that cannot work: Meta blocks marketing-category
# templates to US numbers while still returning success. See src/lib/zapier.ts.
#
# ⚠️ TREAT THIS AS A SECRET. It is unguessable, not authenticated — anyone
# holding the URL can push fake leads to Caroline's phone. Set it in Vercel as
# a normal (hidden) env var, not in config.ts.
#
# Additive, like Resend: unset means `notifyZapier` returns "skipped: …", the
# lead still reaches Caroline by email, and the skip is logged. A missing
# text is never an error the visitor sees.
#
# ⚠️ The Zap must be TURNED ON for this to do anything. An off or deleted Zap
# answers 410 and the log line reads `alert=FAILED: http 410` — that is the
# failure most likely to go unnoticed, because nothing visible breaks.
ZAPIER_LEAD_HOOK_URL=
